SUMMARY:Oct 2nd Community Cuddles
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space. use the link below to reserve
  your **[https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/oct-2nd-community-cuddle](h
 ttps://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/oct-2nd-community-cuddle)**\n\n**This
  is a non-sexual touch based event that invites participants to explore pl
 atonic intimacy in a safe environment** with like-minded people. We respec
 t personal boundaries and through a supportive framework of mutual agreeme
 nts that maximize safety and create a space of easy openness and compassio
 nate connection.\nAt this event we have the chance to normalize touch with
  clear boundaries\; this is a space for respectful\, consent-based touch. 
 We allow ourselves to be seen. We have fun.\nWe welcome people of all back
 grounds\, genders\, ethnicities\, relationship styles\, sexualities\, size
 s\, and ages (18+).\n\n**THE RULES**\n\n1. Clothes stay on for the whole e
 vent.\n2. You do not have to touch anyone at this event.\n3. You must rece
 ive a verbal YES before you touch anyone.\n4. Take care of yourself and th
 ose you choose to interact with.\n5. Speak up if you have a question\, con
 cern\, or if you need assistance with anything during the event.\n6. All e
 motions are welcome- we love vulnerability.\n**WHY CUDDLE?**\nTouch is a b
 asic human need\, and many of us do not get enough\; most people don’t e
 ven know they are missing touch\, or have a way to ask for touch without s
 exualizing it. We believe deeply in the power of touch\, and the importanc
 e of communication and consent in creating a safe space for touch.\nCUDDLI
 NG WITH STRANGERS\nCuddling with strangers sounds weird or scary to most p
 eople. “Will I like it?” “What if someone wants to touch me and I do
 n’t want to?” “What if I say yes and it’s not what I want?” “W
 hat if I really want to touch someone and they say no?” These are all no
 rmal questions. The answer is that this is a space created to ask for exac
 tly what you want\, and receive NOTHING you don’t want. Many people star
 t out nervous at a cuddle event & most are really glad they came.\n\n**Sch
 edule:**\n6:50-7pm: Arrive with snacks to share! Get comfortable\, meet\, 
 mingle\, & snack.\n7:05pm: Welcome Circle- its mandatory. We will set our 
 container\, talk about personal boundaries\, communication\, & consent.\n7
 :15pm: Icebreakers and connective activities.\n8:00pm: Open cuddling! You 
 MUST ask and get a verbal ‘yes’ before touching or cuddling with anybo
 dy at this event. If you are not sure how to do this – great! – we wil
 l talk about it during the welcome circle.\n10:50pm: Closing Circle\, clea
 nup and head home.\n**ETIQUETTE**\n\n\\*ARRIVE ON TIME: It is important th
 at all participants arrive before the Welcome Circle. The Welcome Circle s
 erves the purpose of creating the safe space for consensual\, non-sexual t
 ouch between participants and making sure that everyone is informed about 
 consent.\n\n* Please arrive clean & as scent free as possible.\n\\*BE SOBE
 R: Please do not drink or smoke before or at this event.\n\n**WHAT TO BRIN
 G:** personal water bottle and snacks to share\, a friend\, a date – wha
 tever cuddle accessories you like! The only thing that you are required to
  bring is a clean and sober you.\n\nThese events are not "gender balanced"
 .\n\n**We take individual and group safety seriously!** If you experience\
 , see\, or know that one of our participants is not safe to be at this eve
 nt we want to know about it. We are committed to doing our best to create 
 a safe environment which means that if someone is causing harm (physical o
 r mental) that person is not welcome here (this includes harm that takes p
 lace outside of our events). We stand behind survivors and know that some 
 of our participants are here to heal from touch based trauma.\n\n\\*refund
  policy-\nFull refund if you cancel 7 days before the event or you cancel 
 due to illness\, emergency\, or direct exposure to covid/flu.\nCredit towa
 rds a future event if you cancel more than 3 days before an event.\nNo ref
 und if you cancel within 2 days of the event or no-show.
