SUMMARY:Oct 9th Poly/ENM Spicy/Sensual Snuggle
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space.[ ](https://www.zeffy.com/en-U
 S/ticketing/oct-9th-an-evening-of-sensual-snuggles-for-polyenm-folks)**[CL
 ICK HERE TO PURCHASE YOU TICKET AND RESERVE YOUR SPACE FOR THIS EVENT.](ht
 tps://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/oct-9th-an-evening-of-sensual-snuggles
 -for-polyenm-folks)**[ ](https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/oct-9th-an-
 evening-of-sensual-snuggles-for-polyenm-folks)\n\n**This event is specific
 ally for people who identify as or are curious about poly and ENM relation
 ship. Come by yourself. Come with a friend. Come with a partner. Come with
  your whole polycule!**\n\n**What is a Sensual Snuggle Event?**\nThis is a
  sweet & welcoming event where we practice and use verbal consent to conne
 ct and share touch. We talk about boundaries and practice both saying and 
 receiving a “no”. In this space it is common to see people cuddle\, sh
 are massage\, have their hair brushed\, kiss\, expose nipples\, play\, lau
 gh\, cry\, and be vulnerable. This is a sober space where we can relax and
  connect with other humans who are seeking touch based connection.\nWe str
 ive for this to be a safe event. Safe touch enhances our ability to connec
 t with and trust people. When we are in a space of safety\, we are able to
  relax\, feel comfort\, and be vulnerable.\n\n**Our Agreements:**\n1- We a
 sk for what we want an wait for a yes before touching others.\n2- We say n
 o if we don’t want to do something.\n3- We try to receive a no with grac
 e and not take it personally.\n4- We arrive on time\, clean (as scent free
  as possible)\, and sober.\n5- We keep our pants/shorts on at this event. 
 (Tops are optional\; this is a sensual space\, not a sexual space.)\n6- We
  are here to connect with others. Connection can be verbal\, platonic\, or
  spicy!\n7- We welcome diversity. Isms and Phobias are not welcome here!\n
 \n**Who should attend:**\nPeople who are interested in safely exploring to
 uch and sensuality with strangers. This includes people who are single\, p
 eople who are not single\, couples\, folks who are new to town and looking
  for connection\, people of all/any genders and sexual orientations\, peop
 le of all ages (18 and up). People who understand and respect consent\, wh
 o will take care of themselves and people around them. This event is queer
 -normative. The guest list will include all genders\, orientations\, ages\
 , and personalities. If that’s not your thing… This is not the event f
 or you.\n***Who should NOT attend:***\n-People who are only looking for a 
 sex party.\n-People who do not understand and respect consent.\n-People wh
 o have extreme fear of setting and speaking their personal boundaries\; in
  order to create a safe space we need to know that you will say “no” i
 f you feel a no.\n-People who are homophobic\, racist\, sexist\, ageist\, 
 ableist…\n-People under 18 years of age.\n***Schedule of the Evening***\
 n\n* 6:50pm Doors Open\, Mix & Mingle\n* 7:00pm We gather in a circle to m
 eet each other\, build a container\, cover consent and boundary setting an
 d discuss event agreements. Then we will play a few intimacy building game
 s to meet and connect with other people in the room. Please make sure you 
 arrive on-time!\n* 8:15pm Once the container is built we will have self di
 rected snuggling and sensual interactions until the end of the party.\n* 1
 0:50pm Closing Circle\; a time to re-center and connect as a group to verb
 ally share anything that came up at the event or to voice gratitude to som
 eone(s) you enjoyed interacting with.\n* 11:00pm cleanup & head home\; you
  are welcome to help.\n\n**We take individual and group safety seriously!*
 * If you experience\, see\, or know that one of our participants is not sa
 fe to be at this event we want to know about it. We are committed to doing
  our best to create a safe environment which means that if someone is caus
 ing harm (physical or mental) that person is not welcome here (this includ
 es harm that takes place outside of our events). We stand behind survivors
  and know that some of our participants are here to heal from touch based 
 trauma.\n\nThese events are not "gender balanced"[. Check out our website 
 for more information about this decision. ](http://holdmeavl.com/why-i-don
 t-gender-balance-events/)\n\n**Simple definitions/clarifications-** Platon
 ic- marked by the absence of romance or sex.\nMost of the interactions we 
 have with friends and strangers are platonic.\nSensual- gratification of t
 he senses or the indulgence of appetite.\nWe might feel sensual when we fe
 el someone's breath on our neck or experience a extra long and slow caress
 .\nSexual- having or involving sex.\nOften involving one more more peoples
  genitals\; perhaps seeking orgasm.\n\\*Refund Policy- Full refund if you 
 cancel 7 days before the event or you cancel due to illness\, emergency\, 
 or direct exposure to covid. Credit towards a future event if you cancel m
 ore than 3 days before an event. No refund if you cancel within 2 days of 
 the event or no-show.
