 oy of shared vulnerability in an environment where your authenticity is no
 t just accepted but celebrated. This event is an opportunity to connect wi
 th like-minded individuals who appreciate the simplicity of human touch an
 d the profound impact it can have on our well-being.\n\nExpress yourself i
 n a way that feels true to you\, whether through cozy attire or a touch of
  personal flair. We encourage individuality and self-expression\, creating
  an inclusive space where everyone can be their authentic selves. Dress co
 de is Casual and cozy.\n\nThis is an inclusive environment where we will a
 im to foster the dismantling of and no tolerance of ableism\, fat-shaming\
 , homophobia/transphobia\, sexism\, xenophobia\, classism\, racism & other
  ideas that lead to folks feeling disconnected or unwelcome.\n\n**THE RULE
 S**\n1\\. Pants stay on for the whole event\\.\n2\\. You do not have to to
 uch anyone at this event\\.\n3\\. You must ask permission and receive a ve
 rbal YES before you touch anyone\\. Please be specific in your requests\\.
 \n4\\. If you feel a yes\\\, say YES\\. If you feel a no\\\, say NO\\. If 
 you’re a maybe\\\, say NO\\. You can always change your mind\\.\n5\\. Ge
 t your facilitator if you have a question or concern\\\, or if you need as
 sistance with anything during the event\\.\n6\\. Talking\\\, laughter\\\, 
 silence\\\, silliness\\\, stillness\\\, and crying are welcome\\.\n\n**ETI
 QUETTE**\n\n* ARRIVE ON TIME: It is important that all participants arrive
  before the Welcome Circle.\n* Please be free of strong scents\; many folk
 s would rather not be close to someone who smells of perfume\, essential o
 ils\, or cigarettes\n* BE SOBER: Please do not drink or smoke before or at
  this event.\n\n**WHAT TO BRING:** personal water bottle and snacks to sha
 re. The only thing that you are required to bring is a clean and sober you
 .\n\nWe take individual and group safety seriously! if you experience\, se
 e\, or know that one of our participants is not safe to be at a touch base
 d event we want to know about it. We are committed to doing our best to cr
 eate a safe environment which means that if someone is causing harm (physi
 cal or mental) that person is not welcome here (this includes harm that ta
 kes place outside of our events). We stand behind survivors and know that 
 some of our participants are here to heal from touch based trauma.\n\n\\*r
 efund policy- Full refund if you cancel 7 days before the event or you can
 cel due to illness\, emergency\, or direct exposure to covid. Credit towar
 ds a future event if you cancel more than 3 days before an event. No refun
 d if you cancel within 2 days of the event or no-show.
